      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You make an excellent point; the academic discourse is indeed complex because many \"proven\" studies rely on correlation rather than rigorous causal evidence or clear counterfactuals. While the theoretical potential for a positive business case is undeniable, the empirical support is highly inconsistent, with a significant portion of the data showing neutral or even negative financial outcomes in certain contexts. This uncertainty has forced many stakeholders to shift from seeking a guaranteed \"bottom line\" argument to justifying DEI on broader ethical grounds or specific human capital metrics, acknowledging the field is still in an early stage of validating its economic impact.",
