    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "fair enough. but if the data is that messy and the financial case is unproven, it feels like some companies are basically just checking boxes to avoid being \"cancelled\" rather than actually doing anything beneficial. if there isn't a clear link to profitability, isn't it more accurate to say that most of these programs are just a distraction from actual meritocracy?",
